<html>
  <head>
    <title>Guidance Admin</title>
    <meta name="decorator" content="atl.admin">
    $webResourceManager.requireResource("com.keysight.guidance:guidance-admin-config-resources")
  </head>
  <body>

    <form id="guidance-admin-config" class="aui">

       <h2>Check and Ballot X rendering.</h2>
       <p>The plugin can render the &#10004; and &#10008; glypys in two ways: unicode character or png image.
       The unicode glyph looks better and is scalable, but doesn't show up in the default pdf export from 
       confluence.  The image doesn't look as good, but does show up.  To make matters worse, some plugins
       like ScrollOffice tell the code that a pdf is being generated when it's really creating a word
       document - and the glyph works in the ScrollOffice word file but not the pdf export. Sheesh!</p>
       <div id="group-list-container" class="list-container"></div>
       <br />
       <div class="config-input-container">
          <div class="field-group">
             <div class="checkbox">
                <input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" id="for-html" name="for-html">
                <label for="for-html">Use image rather than glyph for HTML output.</label>
             </div>
             <div class="checkbox">
                <input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" id="for-pdf" name="for-pdf">
                <label for="for-pdf">Use image rather than glyph for PDF output.</label>
             </div>
             <div class="checkbox">
                <input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" id="for-word" name="for-word">
                <label for="for-pdf">Use image rather than glyph for Word output.</label>
             </div>
          </div>
       </div>

    </form>
  </body>
</html>
